<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak VW sees output steady in 1997.</title>
<headline>Slovak VW sees output steady in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen Bratislava s.r.o., the Slovak subsidiary of German car maker Volkswagen AG, plans to keep output at 30,000 cars in 1997, after producing 30,147 cars in 1996, a Slovak VW official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Production in 1996, worth about 18 billion crowns in total, exceeded our original plans by 5,147 cars,&quot; VW manager Jaroslav Holecek told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In 1995, Slovak VW produced 19,685 cars.</p>
</text>
